`tickets/tools/go/validate_test.go` has gaps in its coverage of the
preamble-header validation rules:

**Missing-Created and missing-Author** — The table tests missing-Title (line 47)
but not the other two required headers. All three share the same code path
(`requiredSingletonHeaders`). Adding cases for missing-Created and missing-Author
would confirm the list is complete and catch any future refactoring that drops
one entry.

**`gh#N` deprecated scheme** — The table tests the `gh:owner/repo#N` deprecated
scheme (line 159) but not the bare `gh#N` form. The shell tests cover it
(test_validate.sh forge-ref cases) but there is no Go case.

**`Closed:` with non-empty reason accepted** — The table tests
`Closed:` with empty value (rejected, line 110) but has no case for
`Closed: done` (accepted). Without the positive case, the test cannot
distinguish "Closed: accepted when non-empty" from "Closed: always rejected."
